# serializer version: 1
# name: test_dry_run_starts_no_process
  '''
  Plan for the apply of the plan <plan id> of example-org/infra at <tmp>/repo
    1. EXEC the fetch of origin into <tmp>/repo
         git -C <tmp>/repo -c credential.https://github.com.helper= -c 'credential.https://github.com.helper=!gh auth git-credential' fetch --quiet origin
    2. EXEC whether the default branch of origin holds f5961bd2da6856e31914037c0f048337989dfbe7
         git -C <tmp>/repo merge-base --is-ancestor f5961bd2da6856e31914037c0f048337989dfbe7 refs/remotes/origin/HEAD
    3. EXEC whether origin/main holds f5961bd2da6856e31914037c0f048337989dfbe7
         git -C <tmp>/repo merge-base --is-ancestor f5961bd2da6856e31914037c0f048337989dfbe7 refs/remotes/origin/main  [only if the default branch of origin does not hold the commit]
    4. EXEC the export of f5961bd2da6856e31914037c0f048337989dfbe7 into <tmp>/.data/infra/example-org/infra/plans/<plan id>/applies/<apply id>/project
         git -C <tmp>/repo archive --format=tar '--output=<tmp>/.data/infra/example-org/infra/plans/<plan id>/applies/<apply id>/tree.tar' f5961bd2da6856e31914037c0f048337989dfbe7
    5. EXEC the Ansible inventory of the export
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-inventory -i '<inventory>' --list
    6. EXEC the Ansible config of the export, for its host key checks
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-config dump --format json --only-changed  [only if an agent runs the apply]
    7. EXEC the health of each node in service
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s get nodes -o json
    8. EXEC the install of the pinned collections
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-galaxy collection install -r '<tmp>/.data/infra/example-org/infra/plans/<plan id>/applies/<apply id>/project/collections/requirements.yml' -p '<collections folder>'  [only if the repo has collections/requirements.yml and no install of it is kept]
    9. EXEC the run of the hosts with no disruptive class
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-runner run '<tmp>/.data/infra/example-org/infra/plans/<plan id>/applies/<apply id>' --playbook ansible/playbooks/03_k3s.yaml --ident '<ident>' --limit 'node-4.example.com:!<offline group>' --quiet '--cmdline=-v -i '"'"'<inventory>'"'"' -e '"'"'ansible_ssh_private_key_file=<key of devops ssh>'"'"''
   10. EXEC the node of node-3.example.com before the drain
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s get node '<node of node-3.example.com>' -o json
   11. EXEC the server dry run of the drain of node-3.example.com
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s drain '<node of node-3.example.com>' --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data --timeout=30s --dry-run=server
   12. EXEC the drain of node-3.example.com
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s drain '<node of node-3.example.com>' --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data --timeout=180s
   13. EXEC the fresh check of node-3.example.com, which must give its plan
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-runner run '<tmp>/.data/infra/example-org/infra/plans/<plan id>/applies/<apply id>' --playbook ansible/playbooks/03_k3s.yaml --ident '<ident>' --limit 'node-3.example.com:!<offline group>' --quiet '--cmdline=--check --diff -v -i '"'"'<inventory>'"'"' -e '"'"'ansible_ssh_private_key_file=<key of devops ssh>'"'"''
   14. EXEC the run of node-3.example.com
         <tmp>/user-data/tools/ansible-core/2.22.0/bin/ansible-runner run '<tmp>/.data/infra/example-org/infra/plans/<plan id>/applies/<apply id>' --playbook ansible/playbooks/03_k3s.yaml --ident '<ident>' --limit 'node-3.example.com:!<offline group>' --quiet '--cmdline=-v -i '"'"'<inventory>'"'"' -e '"'"'ansible_ssh_private_key_file=<key of devops ssh>'"'"''
   15. EXEC Ready and the GPUs of node-3.example.com
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s get node '<node of node-3.example.com>' -o json  [repeated once each poll interval until it passes twice or the wait ends]
   16. EXEC the health of each node in service
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s get nodes -o json  [repeated once each poll interval until it passes twice or the wait ends]
   17. EXEC the uncordon of node-3.example.com
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s uncordon '<node of node-3.example.com>'  [only if the node was schedulable before the drain]
   18. EXEC the node of node-3.example.com after the apply
         kubectl --context homelab-example --request-timeout=30s get node '<node of node-3.example.com>' -o json
   19. WRITE the audit record infra.apply
  Each disruptive host runs alone in plan order. The node of a host stays cordoned when it was cordoned before. The first failure stops the apply.
  
  '''
